- `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models` — 200, ~842 KB of catalogue, **0 occurrences** of `qoduck`.
- `https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/models` — 200, ~569 KB of catalogue, **0 occurrences** of `qoduck`.
- `https://huggingface.co/api/models?search=qoduck` — 200, **empty result array** (no weights, no repo).
- Artificial Analysis catalogue (285 models, 2026-11-11 snapshot) — **no `qoduck` entry**.
- `https://stealthmodels.com/qwen-4` — 200, the third-party tracker entry dated 2026-11-07: tokenizer probe placing Qoduck in the Qwen family, reported 1M window switch, normal price matching Qwen3.8-Max, "no public API", and Qoduck listed among the **unconfirmed** Qwen 4 look-alikes alongside Kalmia and Kerria.
- `https://startupfortune.com/alibabas-qoder-makes-a-mystery-coding-model-called-qoduck-free-to-use/` — 200: "Alibaba's Qoder launched the stealth model Qoduck on November 7, free within a daily quota for individuals. Its maker and benchmarks remain undisclosed."
- `https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2026-11-09/doc-iniyaqqe6537597.shtml` — 200: Chinese coverage of the Qoder stealth-model launch, identity undisclosed, free for three days with no credits consumed.
- DuckDuckGo searches for `QoDuck Qoder model Alibaba stealth` and for Qoder/Qoduck benchmark results — no vendor benchmark table, no harness report, no scorecard for the model itself.

### Conflicting evidence (vendor vs independent) and how it was resolved

There is no vendor benchmark claim to reconcile with an independent measurement, because neither exists. The only conflicts are internal to the record: (1) Qoder's documentation publishes the credit rate and promotion window but **no context size, modality list or model identity**, while the repository's curated metadata asserts 1M/64K, text+image in, text+code out and an "OpenCode Zen rate" — all of which are **unverifiable**, since no Zen, OpenRouter, Vercel or models.dev entry exists; and (2) third-party trackers assert a 1M window and a Qwen-family tokenizer while carefully labelling the Qwen 4 identification **unconfirmed**. These claims were therefore recorded as reported-but-unsourced and not used as evidence.

### Notes on identity

- **Publicly documented:** the name, the host product, the promotion mechanics and the dates — nothing else.
- **Attribution-by-telemetry:** partial and third-party only (Qwen-family tokenizer fingerprint, reported knowledge-check result).
- **Endpoint still live?** No. The promotion ended on 2026-11-11 and Qoder's FAQ says the model is removed when it ends; no catalog still carries the id.
- **Why this is a legitimate finding:** a documented absence is still a finding. Because not one verified public benchmark number exists for this id, the file is saved with the `.md.excluded` suffix so that no invented number can enter the averages.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

No scores are assigned for this entry. Every dimension of the rubric (tool use, reasoning, context window, multimodal, coding, cost efficiency) depends on a verified measurement or a documented catalogue row, and for `qoduck` none exists: the raw-benchmarks section above is entirely "no verified public score found". Publishing a scored file would mean inventing a benchmark or passing curated metadata off as sourced fact, so this file is intentionally saved as `MiniMax_M3.1_Flash.md.excluded` and contributes nothing to the averages.

